WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.787
The teaching database includes several examples because reshaping appears in many domains.

00:00:04.787 --> 00:00:07.332
Admissions and sales begin in long form.

00:00:07.332 --> 00:00:10.607
Monthly sales and patient metrics begin in wide form.

00:00:10.607 --> 00:00:14.472
Survey responses and grades are useful for matrix-style pivots.

00:00:14.472 --> 00:00:19.307
The different examples help you focus on the reshape pattern rather than memorizing one dataset.

00:00:19.307 --> 00:00:24.482
Connect this idea to a machine-learning workflow converting wide measurements into tidy long data.

00:00:24.482 --> 00:00:30.747
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:30.747 --> 00:00:35.397
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:35.397 --> 00:00:40.397
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:40.397 --> 00:00:45.680
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
